    {
      "name": "mobile-onboarding-setup",
      "volatile": true,
      "reason": "Accepted disclosed gap, whole-screen volatile: ~30px (0.009%) sub-pixel rasterization noise at the SetupLauncher card's rounded border, surviving this project's deterministic-rendering Chromium flags. Three hypotheses tried and DISPROVED (a live /api/system/status race — closed by this screen's own waitSettled guard; a CSS animation on the card — it has none; a --dock-slot-size-driven layout race — measured byte-identical across 4 repeated captures, both the custom property and the card's own boundingBox()) before concluding host-dependent sub-pixel rasterization. Review MED-3 (fix round) independently RE-CONFIRMED the non-determinism still reproduces post-MED-1-leak-fix (9 standalone/mixed-order captures landed on two distinct stable sha256 values, 6-of-9 vs 3-of-9, no correlation to run order or anything under this suite's control) — see the screen's own afterGoto comment in tests/screenshots.spec.ts. A reference PNG is committed at tests/screenshots.baseline/mobile-onboarding-setup.png for human eyeballing only; screenshot-diff.mjs never stores or reads an image for a volatile entry (see runBaseline/runDiff), so the comparator always skips it. Follow-up if this recurs on another screen: a region-scoped comparison that excludes just the card's rounded-border pixels instead of exempting the whole tile."
    },
